From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a browser window opens under a Wayland host

At Chromium 160 every browser window crashed while Ozone/Wayland created
it. `BrowserDesktopWindowTreeHostLinux::CalculateInsetsInDIP` now asks
`SupportsClientFrameShadow()` first, which reads `platform_window()`, and
`WaylandWindow::Initialize` asks for those insets while
`DesktopWindowTreeHostPlatform::Init` is still creating the window, so the
host does not hold it yet and the read is a null dereference. The engine
guards that run the shell nested in a Wayland compositor hit it at once.

- `SupportsClientFrameShadow`: with no platform window yet there are no
  client-side shadows, so the insets are empty, as they are for a window
  without a custom frame.
---
 .../ui/views/frame/browser_desktop_window_tree_host_linux.cc  | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_desktop_window_tree_host_linux.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_desktop_window_tree_host_linux.cc
index 1200a60..f3fa512 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_desktop_window_tree_host_linux.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/frame/browser_desktop_window_tree_host_linux.cc
@@ -148,7 +148,9 @@ void BrowserDesktopWindowTreeHostLinux::TabDraggingKindChanged(
 }
 
 bool BrowserDesktopWindowTreeHostLinux::SupportsClientFrameShadow() const {
-  return platform_window()->CanSetDecorationInsets() &&
+  // The Wayland window asks for its insets while it is being created, before
+  // this host holds it.
+  return platform_window() && platform_window()->CanSetDecorationInsets() &&
          views::Widget::IsWindowCompositingSupported();
 }
 
